        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe rename/consolidation is thorough and consistent across every layer (model, function, event, all four schemas, YAML wiring, OpenAPI), and the construction logic moved cleanly into `AssignMemberId` with cohesive private `sha256UpperHex8`/`luhn` helpers. Two structural points keep it from being clean:\n\n1. **Duplicated, unexplained memberId-segment arithmetic in `Owner`.** `getFiscalYear()` and `getLocality()` both hard-code the fixed suffix width `11` (and `getFiscalYear` additionally `9`) and do bare substring-from-the-end math to carve out the FY and REGION segments. The memberId layout (CHK 1 + HASH8 8 + FY 2) is now encoded as magic offsets in two separate methods that must change in lockstep if the format ever shifts \u2014 and the two length guards even differ (`>= 11` vs `> 11`) for no self-evident reason. Introduce named constants (e.g. `CHK_WIDTH`/`HASH8_WIDTH`/`FY_WIDTH`, or a single `SUFFIX_WIDTH = 11`) or a small private segment-extraction helper alongside `memberIdBase()`, so the format is described in one place rather than inferred from literals. This is the format-knowledge counterpart to `AssignMemberId` building `region + fy + hash8 + chk`; right now that knowledge is split and partly implicit.\n\n2. **`getPrimaryIdentifier()` is now a pure alias of `getMemberId()`.** Its documented reason to exist was the \"customerCode today, memberId later\" seam so downstream consumers would follow the switch automatically. That switch has now happened, so the method is just `return this.memberId`, duplicating the real accessor, and its own javadoc now says it *is* the memberId. Either fold the audit/event back onto `getMemberId()` directly, or keep `getPrimaryIdentifier()` only if you genuinely want a lasting semantic seam \u2014 but as written it's indirection that no longer earns its keep, which a maintainer will find puzzling next to the identically-valued `getMemberId()`."
